---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { useTranslations } from '../../i18n/ui';
const lang = 'en';
const t = useTranslations(lang);
---
<Base lang="en" title="RPA Readiness Checklist — geoli.eu" description="Evaluate your processes and determine which are ready for robotic process automation.">
  <style>
    .guide {
      max-width: 900px;
      margin: 3rem auto;
      padding: 0 1rem;
    }
    .guide h1 { font-size: 2rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
    .guide section { margin: 3rem 0; }
    .guide h2 { font-size: 1.4rem; margin-top: 2rem; margin-bottom: 0.8rem; }
    .guide h3 { font-size: 1.1rem; margin-top: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.6rem; }
    .guide p { line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: var(--text-soft); }
    .guide li { margin-bottom: 0.8rem; color: var(--text-muted); }
    .guide ul { margin-left: 1.5rem; }
    .checklist-item {
      background: var(--bg-card);
      padding: 1rem;
      border-radius: 8px;
      margin: 0.8rem 0;
      border-left: 4px solid var(--indigo);
    }
    .checklist-item label {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 0.8rem;
      cursor: pointer;
      font-weight: 500;
    }
    .checklist-item input[type="checkbox"] {
      width: 20px;
      height: 20px;
      cursor: pointer;
    }
    .download-btn {
      display: inline-block;
      padding: 0.8rem 1.5rem;
      background: var(--indigo);
      color: white;
      border-radius: 8px;
      text-decoration: none;
      margin: 2rem 0;
      font-weight: 500;
      border: none;
      cursor: pointer;
    }
    .download-btn:hover { opacity: 0.9; }
  </style>

  <article class="guide">
    <h1>RPA Readiness Checklist</h1>
    <p style="font-size: 1.1rem; color: var(--text-soft);">Use this checklist to evaluate whether your processes are suitable for robotic process automation. Score honestly—the result will guide your automation roadmap.</p>

    <button onclick="window.print()" class="download-btn">Print / Save as PDF</button>

    <section>
      <h2>Process Characteristics (40 points)</h2>
      <p>A good RPA candidate is rule-based, high-volume, and deterministic. These questions help identify such processes.</p>

      <div class="checklist-item">
        <label>
          <input type="checkbox" />
          <span>The process follows clear, documented rules (if input A, do X; if input B, do Y)</span>
        </label>
      </div>

      <div class="checklist-item">
        <label>
          <input type="checkbox" />
          <span>The process is repetitive and high-volume (100+ instances per month)</span>
        </label>
      </div>

      <div class="checklist-item">
        <label>
          <input type="checkbox" />
          <span>Most steps are deterministic (not dependent on human judgment)</span>
        </label>
      </div>

      <div class="checklist-item">
        <label>
          <input type="checkbox" />
          <span>The process has been stable for at least 6 months (not changing frequently)</span>
        </label>
      </div>

      <div class="checklist-item">
        <label>
          <input type="checkbox" />
          <span>Input data is structured or semi-structured (forms, spreadsheets, databases, not unstructured text)</span>
        </label>
      </div>

      <div class="checklist-item">
        <label>
          <input type="checkbox" />
          <span>The process touches 3-8 systems (not 15+ which adds complexity)</span>
        </label>
      </div>

      <div class="checklist-item">
        <label>
          <input type="checkbox" />
          <span>Exception rate is below 5% (bot can handle 95% of cases; exceptions are rare)</span>
        </label>
      </div>

      <div class="checklist-item">
        <label>
          <input type="checkbox" />
          <span>The process does not require complex decision-making or judgment calls</span>
        </label>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>System & Technology Requirements (30 points)</h2>
      <p>RPA works best in stable, well-connected technology environments. These questions assess readiness.</p>

      <div class="checklist-item">
        <label>
          <input type="checkbox" />
          <span>All systems the bot needs to access have stable, documented APIs or UI-based access</span>
        </label>
      </div>

      <div class="checklist-item">
        <label>
          <input type="checkbox" />
          <span>Systems are not constantly changing (updates/migrations on the horizon?)</span>
        </label>
      </div>

      <div class="checklist-item">
        <label>
          <input type="checkbox" />
          <span>You can run bot-specific service accounts with appropriate permissions</span>
        </label>
      </div>

      <div class="checklist-item">
        <label>
          <input type="checkbox" />
          <span>Your infrastructure can support a bot (server, scheduler, or cloud agent)</span>
        </label>
      </div>

      <div class="checklist-item">
        <label>
          <input type="checkbox" />
          <span>Network connectivity is reliable (bot won't be blocked by firewalls or timeouts)</span>
        </label>
      </div>

      <div class="checklist-item">
        <label>
          <input type="checkbox" />
          <span>IT/Security approves bot automation (no policy blockers)</span>
        </label>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Organization & Governance (20 points)</h2>
      <p>RPA success depends on organizational readiness, not just technology. These factors matter.</p>

      <div class="checklist-item">
        <label>
          <input type="checkbox" />
          <span>Process owner is committed and available for implementation (not passive)</span>
        </label>
      </div>

      <div class="checklist-item">
        <label>
          <input type="checkbox" />
          <span>You have clear business case with ROI metrics (cost savings, time saved, error reduction)</span>
        </label>
      </div>

      <div class="checklist-item">
        <label>
          <input type="checkbox" />
          <span>Change management plan exists (team knows what's changing, when, and why)</span>
        </label>
      </div>

      <div class="checklist-item">
        <label>
          <input type="checkbox" />
          <span>You have designated time for testing and validation (not rushing to production)</span>
        </label>
      </div>

      <div class="checklist-item">
        <label>
          <input type="checkbox" />
          <span>Team has capacity to maintain the bot post-launch (not a one-off project)</span>
        </label>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Data & Compliance (10 points)</h2>
      <p>Data handling and compliance are critical. These questions flag risks.</p>

      <div class="checklist-item">
        <label>
          <input type="checkbox" />
          <span>Process data does not include sensitive PII (or if it does, you have encryption/masking)</span>
        </label>
      </div>

      <div class="checklist-item">
        <label>
          <input type="checkbox" />
          <span>Compliance requirements are clear and documented (GDPR, HIPAA, audit trails, etc.)</span>
        </label>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Scoring</h2>
      <p style="margin: 1.5rem 0;">Count the checkboxes you marked as true. Compare to the scale below:</p>

      <table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 1.5rem 0;">
        <tr style="background: var(--bg-card); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);">
          <td style="padding: 1rem; font-weight: 600;">90-100 points</td>
          <td style="padding: 1rem; color: var(--emerald);">🟢 Highly suitable for RPA</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);">
          <td style="padding: 1rem; font-weight: 600;">70-89 points</td>
          <td style="padding: 1rem; color: var(--accent-soft);">🟡 Good candidate (address gaps first)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);">
          <td style="padding: 1rem; font-weight: 600;">50-69 points</td>
          <td style="padding: 1rem; color: var(--warn-text);">🟠 Moderate fit (requires rework)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td style="padding: 1rem; font-weight: 600;">Below 50 points</td>
          <td style="padding: 1rem; color: var(--err-text);">🔴 Not recommended for RPA</td>
        </tr>
      </table>

      <h3>What to do with your score:</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>90-100:</strong> Proceed to pilot. Low risk, high ROI likely.</li>
        <li><strong>70-89:</strong> Good candidate. Document gaps and mitigation plan. Example: If systems change frequently, agree on a 6-month stability window before automating.</li>
        <li><strong>50-69:</strong> Consider refactoring the process first. Simplify rules, clean up data, or reduce system count before automating. Then re-evaluate.</li>
        <li><strong>Below 50:</strong> Not ready. Focus on process improvement first. RPA amplifies chaos; it doesn't fix it.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Next Steps</h2>
      <p>If your score is 70+:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Document the process in detail (flowchart, decision points, exception cases)</li>
        <li>Measure baseline metrics (time per case, error rate, volume)</li>
        <li>Identify the bot's specific responsibilities (which steps it will automate)</li>
        <li>Plan the pilot: scope, timeline, success criteria, roll-out plan</li>
        <li>Engage an RPA partner or internal team to build and test</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>
